pip is fully working again. Here's what was wrong and what I did:

**Problem:** The `pip` package's actual source code (`/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/`) was missing from your system, but the stale metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info/`) remained. This made `ensurepip` think pip was already installed and skip re-extracting it, so `pip3` would always fail with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.

**Fix:** I removed the orphaned `.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which extracted the bundled pip wheel back into place. pip 24.3.1 is now functional and can install packages.

